/******************************************************************************
 * JPA RELATIONSHIPS - QUICK REFERENCE
 ******************************************************************************/

/*
===============================================================================
1. BUSINESS PARENT vs JPA OWNING SIDE
===============================================================================

These are NOT the same.

Business Parent
---------------
Real-world relationship.

Example:

Department
    |
    +---- Alice
    +---- Bob
    +---- Charlie

Department is the business parent.
Employees are business children.

JPA Owning Side
---------------
Entity containing @JoinColumn.

Rule:

@JoinColumn  ==> Owning Side
mappedBy     ==> Inverse Side

Owning side updates the foreign key.
*/


/*
===============================================================================
2. @OneToOne
===============================================================================

Foreign key can exist in EITHER table.

Example 1

Person
-------
id   name   passport_id
1    Mohan      100

Passport
--------
id   number
100  TN123456

Person owns the relationship
(Person contains @JoinColumn)


---------------------------------------------------

Example 2

Person
-------
id   name
1    Mohan

Passport
--------
id   number     person_id
100  TN123456       1

Passport owns the relationship
(Passport contains @JoinColumn)


Rule:
Either entity can own a OneToOne relationship.
*/


/*
===============================================================================
3. @OneToMany / @ManyToOne
===============================================================================

Database

Department
----------
id   name
1    IT

Employee
--------
id   name      department_id
1    Alice          1
2    Bob            1
3    Charlie        1


Business Parent
---------------
Department

Business Child
--------------
Employee

JPA Owning Side
---------------
Employee
(because Employee has @JoinColumn)

Inverse Side
------------
Department
(because Department has mappedBy)


Typical Mapping

@Entity
class Department {

    @OneToMany(
        mappedBy = "department",
        cascade = CascadeType.ALL,
        orphanRemoval = true
    )
    List<Employee> employees;
}

@Entity
class Employee {

    @ManyToOne
    @JoinColumn(name = "department_id")
    Department department;
}
*/


/*
===============================================================================
4. CASCADE
===============================================================================

Cascade direction depends ONLY on where cascade is written.

@OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL)

Department -------------> Employee

Example

Department
----------
1 IT

Employees
---------
Alice
Bob
Charlie

departmentRepository.save(department)

Result

INSERT Department
INSERT Alice
INSERT Bob
INSERT Charlie


departmentRepository.delete(department)

Result

DELETE Alice
DELETE Bob
DELETE Charlie
DELETE Department

Cascade does NOT determine the owning side.
*/


/*
===============================================================================
5. ORPHAN REMOVAL
===============================================================================

Department

IT
├── Alice
├── Bob
└── Charlie

Java

department.getEmployees().remove(bob);

With orphanRemoval = true

Database becomes

IT
├── Alice
└── Charlie

Bob is deleted from Employee table.

Hibernate executes

DELETE FROM employee
WHERE id = Bob


Difference

Cascade REMOVE

Delete Department

Result

Department deleted
All Employees deleted


Orphan Removal

Department still exists

Only Bob removed

Result

IT
├── Alice
└── Charlie
*/


/*
===============================================================================
6. DATABASE FOREIGN KEY
===============================================================================

Department
----------
id
1

Employee
--------
id   name     department_id
1    Alice        1
2    Bob          1

Employee contains department_id.

Therefore

Employee is the JPA owning side.

Owning side updates department_id.
*/


/*
===============================================================================
7. DATABASE ON DELETE CASCADE
===============================================================================

FOREIGN KEY(department_id)
REFERENCES department(id)
ON DELETE CASCADE

Database

Department
----------
1 IT

Employee
--------
Alice
Bob

Execute

DELETE FROM department WHERE id=1;

Database automatically deletes

Alice
Bob

This is DATABASE Cascade.

It is NOT the same as

CascadeType.ALL

which is handled by Hibernate.
*/


/*
===============================================================================
8. MEMORY TRICKS
===============================================================================

Business Parent
    -> Real-world ownership

@JoinColumn
    -> JPA Owning Side

mappedBy
    -> Inverse Side

cascade
    -> Operation propagation direction

orphanRemoval
    -> Delete child removed from parent's collection

ON DELETE CASCADE
    -> Database performs delete

CascadeType.ALL
    -> Hibernate performs delete
*/


/*
===============================================================================
9. INTERVIEW RULES
===============================================================================

@OneToOne
    Either side can own.

@ManyToOne
    Usually owning side.

@OneToMany
    Usually inverse side.

@JoinColumn
    Owning side.

mappedBy
    Inverse side.

Remember

Business Parent != JPA Owning Side

Business Parent = Real-world ownership.

JPA Owning Side = Entity managing the foreign key.
===============================================================================
*/